      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T23:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can assume that `SHA256_update` will ever be called for a given context: it\u0027s legal to hash a zero-byte message without ever calling `update`.\n\nThe software implementation in sha256.c looks like it does what I\u0027m saying, by doing padding only in `SHA256_final`; it looks almost like this implementation makes a number of assumptions about the usage (regarding the pattern of blocks passed to `update`) that are true for the vboot use case, but aren\u0027t generally true.",
      "parentUuid": "ad64cb93_a8f94f09",
